# oracle: fix wall/region/ees (cut down from examples/PACKAGES/ees/in.fix_wall_region, Data_region): three ellipsoids outside a
# side-out block region (the surface contacts of the block faces within the cutoff), resquared pair, nve/asphere, 400 steps.
# Per-atom compare of x, v, f and the energy/force-sum vector of the fix.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# measured with native LAMMPS: max relative error below 1e-13 (per-atom and thermo)
# oracle-inputs: w133mf_region_ees.data
# native: b332f28 built with the installed lmp (EXTRA-FIX)
units lj
atom_style ellipsoid
boundary p p p
read_data w133mf_region_ees.data
region the_wall block 20. 40. 20. 40. 20. 40. side out
pair_style resquared 1
pair_coeff 1 1 10.0 1.0 0.5 0.5 4 0.5 0.5 4 1
timestep 0.0005
fix EES_block all wall/region/ees the_wall 10. 1. 20
fix NVE all nve/asphere
compute temp all temp/asphere
thermo_modify temp temp
thermo_style custom step temp press etotal f_EES_block f_EES_block[1] f_EES_block[3]
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo 100
run 400
